passage:
(MandiSpeakers)-[USE]->(BanglaInPrayers)
// SENTCE REF: In church I use Bangla in conducting prayers.
// SOURCE: The Chittagong University Journal of Social Sciences

(MandiSpeakers)-[PREFER_TO_USE]->(MandiAtHome)
// SENTCE REF: We do some prayers every evening at home when we prefer to use Mandi.
// SOURCE: The Chittagong University Journal of Social Sciences

(MandiSpeakers)-[ORGANIZE_PRAYERS_AND_RITUALS]->(TwiceAWek)
// SENTCE REF: Mandi is used on those two days.
// SOURCE: The Chittagong University Journal of Social Sciences

(MandiSpeakers)-[FEEL_SPIRITUAL]->(BanglaPrayers)
// SENTCE REF: The Mandi language is oral, and they use the Roman alphabet to write t. It is interesting to note here that they cannot feel spiritual if they do their prayer in Mandi language.
// SOURCE: The Chittagong University Journal of Social Sciences
